{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017kH4R8p1UBDZBpQ2ypTEx5","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/runbooks/onboard-repo.md:90:dry-run only.\ndocs/site/operations/gate-2-runbook.md:49:unset ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN ARD_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\ndocs/site/operations/gate-2-runbook.md:50:export ARD_GITHUB_APP_ID=5877373\ndocs/site/operations/gate-2-runbook.md:58:`ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN` must stay unset: a personal token makes the client\ndocs/site/getting-started.md:31:Give `ard serve` the App through its environment: `ARD_GITHUB_APP_ID`, `ARD_GITHUB_INSTALLATION_ID` and the key as `ARD_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE` (a path) or `ARD_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY`.\ndocs/proposal.md:525:- **Identity: a GitHub App, not a PAT.** Installation tokens expire hourly and are scoped to contents, issues and pull requests (read and write), plus checks (read and write) and commit statuses (read). The merger reads check runs (checks: read), commit statuses (commit statuses: read) and the branch rules (metadata). The merger needs read to see required checks; the owner kept write so ard can later publish its own check runs, but nothing in Phase 1 writes checks. Leaving out the `workflows` permission makes GitHub itself reject any push that edits `.github/workflows/`, a second backstop behind a guard that already refuses all of `.github/`, and it also keeps the bot from editing the bot-commit audit. The scratch-repo run (#85) confirmed that GitHub rejects such a push (\"refusing to allow a GitHub App to create or update workflow ... without `workflows` permission\"), and that these work with exactly this permission set: label writes, PR create, review and mark-ready, pinning the status issue, and timeline and collaborator-permission reads. A personal token (`ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN`) is accepted only for local `--dry-run` development, and the client is then made read-only so no write can reach GitHub.\n\noverrides:                   # only what differs from convention\n  scanners/cve:             { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/lts:             { every: 7d, max_open: 5, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/docs:            { every: 3d, max_open: 3, group_size: 10, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/error-codes:     { every: 24h, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/missing-tests:   { every: 24h, max_open: 5, group_size: 10, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/trufflehog:      { every: 24h, max_open: 5, group_size: 1, autoclose: true, route: needs-human, timeout: 30m }\n  scanners/trufflehog-history: { every: 7d, max_open: 5, group_size: 1, autoclose: false, route: needs-human, timeout: 60m }\n  scanners/lint:            { every: 24h, max_open: 3, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }\n  triage/lead:              { sidecar: vpe-specs, timeout: 15m, model: claude-opus-5-5 }","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65048bc8-546a-4025-a94f-356c42be7752","uuid":"51060dd1-b9c3-41a1-b546-19750f2b2793","timestamp":"2026-11-25T20:53:29.609Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"docs/runbooks/onboard-repo.md:90:dry-run only.\ndocs/site/operations/gate-2-runbook.md:49:unset ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN ARD_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\ndocs/site/operations/gate-2-runbook.md:50:export ARD_GITHUB_APP_ID=5877373\ndocs/site/operations/gate-2-runbook.md:58:`ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN` must stay unset: a personal token makes the client\ndocs/site/getting-started.md:31:Give `ard serve` the App through its environment: `ARD_GITHUB_APP_ID`, `ARD_GITHUB_INSTALLATION_ID` and the key as `ARD_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE` (a path) or `ARD_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY`.\ndocs/proposal.md:525:- **Identity: a GitHub App, not a PAT.** Installation tokens expire hourly and are scoped to contents, issues and pull requests (read and write), plus checks (read and write) and commit statuses (read). The merger reads check runs (checks: read), commit statuses (commit statuses: read) and the branch rules (metadata). The merger needs read to see required checks; the owner kept write so ard can later publish its own check runs, but nothing in Phase 1 writes checks. Leaving out the `workflows` permission makes GitHub itself reject any push that edits `.github/workflows/`, a second backstop behind a guard that already refuses all of `.github/`, and it also keeps the bot from editing the bot-commit audit. The scratch-repo run (#85) confirmed that GitHub rejects such a push (\"refusing to allow a GitHub App to create or update workflow ... without `workflows` permission\"), and that these work with exactly this permission set: label writes, PR create, review and mark-ready, pinning the status issue, and timeline and collaborator-permission reads. A personal token (`ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN`) is accepted only for local `--dry-run` development, and the client is then made read-only so no write can reach GitHub.\n\noverrides:                   # only what differs from convention\n  scanners/cve:             { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/lts:             { every: 7d, max_open: 5, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/docs:            { every: 3d, max_open: 3, group_size: 10, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/error-codes:     { every: 24h, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/missing-tests:   { every: 24h, max_open: 5, group_size: 10, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/trufflehog:      { every: 24h, max_open: 5, group_size: 1, autoclose: true, route: needs-human, timeout: 30m }\n  scanners/trufflehog-history: { every: 7d, max_open: 5, group_size: 1, autoclose: false, route: needs-human, timeout: 60m }\n  scanners/lint:            { every: 24h, max_open: 3, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }\n  triage/lead:              { sidecar: vpe-specs, timeout: 15m, model: claude-opus-5-5 }","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017kH4R8p1UBDZBpQ2ypTEx5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reas