{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018QnDzqYe9bE5f8RXWjuNvQ","type":"tool_result","content":"intended effects to `effects.jsonl`. Soak and read the ledger, then start\n`ard serve` without the flag.\n\nIn the cluster, add an entry for the repository to the instances list in the\ndeployment repository (check the key name in that repository's docs). Live agent\njobs in the cluster need #54; until it lands, run the cluster instance in\ndry-run only.\n\n## 7. Optional: a shared roles repository\n\n`roles_repo: {repo: <owner>/<name>, ref: <ref>}` in `.ard/config.yaml` loads\n\nKeep this in a file outside the repo and source it in the shell that runs ard:\n\n```bash\n# ard-env.sh\nunset ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN ARD_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\nexport ARD_GITHUB_APP_ID=5877373\nexport ARD_GITHUB_INSTALLATION_ID=184746846\nexport ARD_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE=\"$HOME/.ard/keys/ard-scratch.pem\"\nexport ARD_AGENT_AUTH=oauth\nCLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=$(op read \"op://Private/claude setup-token/credential\") || return 1\nexport CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\n```\n\n`ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN` must stay unset: a personal token makes the client\nread-only and is refused outside `--dry-run`.\n\n## Stage A: smoke run on ard-scratch\n\nGoal: one issue goes `ard:pending` → triage → approval → worker → draft PR →\neng-review, and a human merges it. About an hour and a few dollars.\n| Commit statuses | Read |\n| Metadata | Read |\n\nDo **not** grant `workflows`. Without it GitHub itself rejects any push that edits `.github/workflows/`. Install the App on the target repository, then note the App ID and installation ID and download the private key (a `.pem` file; keep it mode 0600).\n\nGive `ard serve` the App through its environment: `ARD_GITHUB_APP_ID`, `ARD_GITHUB_INSTALLATION_ID` and the key as `ARD_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE` (a path) or `ARD_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY`.\n\n## 2. Initialise the repository\n\n```sh\nard init\n44:Install the App, run `ard init`, commit and merge the tree, run `ard setup`, fix any manual rows it reports, try `ard serve --dry-run`, then go live. See [Getting started](docs/site/getting-started.md).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65048bc8-546a-4025-a94f-356c42be7752","uuid":"e3ca86d9-29af-4a21-9975-164fae9e85e9","timestamp":"2026-11-25T20:53:30.882Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"intended effects to `effects.jsonl`. Soak and read the ledger, then start\n`ard serve` without the flag.\n\nIn the cluster, add an entry for the repository to the instances list in the\ndeployment repository (check the key name in that repository's docs). Live agent\njobs in the cluster need #54; until it lands, run the cluster instance in\ndry-run only.\n\n## 7. Optional: a shared roles repository\n\n`roles_repo: {repo: <owner>/<name>, ref: <ref>}` in `.ard/config.yaml` loads\n\nKeep this in a file outside the repo and source it in the shell that runs ard:\n\n```bash\n# ard-env.sh\nunset ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN ARD_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\nexport ARD_GITHUB_APP_ID=5877373\nexport ARD_GITHUB_INSTALLATION_ID=184746846\nexport ARD_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE=\"$HOME/.ard/keys/ard-scratch.pem\"\nexport ARD_AGENT_AUTH=oauth\nCLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=$(op read \"op://Private/claude setup-token/credential\") || return 1\nexport CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\n```\n\n`ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN` must stay unset: a personal token makes the client\nread-only and is refused outside `--dry-run`.\n\n## Stage A: smoke run on ard-scratch\n\nGoal: one issue goes `ard:pending` → triage → approval → worker → draft PR →\neng-review, and a human merges it. About an hour and a few dollars.\n| Commit statuses | Read |\n| Metadata | Read |\n\nDo **not** grant `workflows`. Without it GitHub itself rejects any push that edits `.github/workflows/`. Install the App on the target repository, then note the App ID and installation ID and download the private key (a `.pem` file; keep it mode 0600).\n\nGive `ard serve` the App through its environment: `ARD_GITHUB_APP_ID`, `ARD_GITHUB_INSTALLATION_ID` and the key as `ARD_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE` (a path) or `ARD_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY`.\n\n## 2. Initialise the repository\n\n```sh\nard init\n44:Install the App, run `ard init`, commit and merge the tree, run `ard setup`, fix any manual rows it reports, try `ard serve --dry-run`, then go live. See [Getting started](docs/site/getting-started.md).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018QnDzqYe9bE5f8RXWjuNvQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
