{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQKPGeCXkH2rJRLXEbvZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've implemented the change for #302. `go test ./...` passes. `go vet ./...` prints only a parse note for an existing testdata file. The report is written to `.ard/302/worker-engineer.md`.\n\n- **Startup check:** `ard serve` now checks the credentials against the repo before any loop starts. If something is missing, it exits non-zero with one line naming it. It logs `github.connect` once on success. The code is in `internal/github/connect.go`, with the typed error in `errors.go`.\n- **PAT for live runs:** `ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN` now works without `--dry-run`.\n- **`gh` fallback:** with no credentials set, `ard serve` handles three cases.\n  - `gh` is absent: it prints both setup options and exits.\n  - `gh` is logged out: it prints the `gh auth login` command and exits.\n  - `gh` is logged in: it reads the token once and holds it in memory. The token goes only to the redactors, never to logs, files or agent environments. The code is in `internal/github/ghcli.go`.\n- **`ard config check`:** it now prints a `github auth:` line saying app, token or none. It never runs `gh` or touches the network.\n- **Self-review decision:** I changed no merger logic. Reviews are already comment-only. Under a PAT, the token user's own approval doesn't count for protected paths, so a different write-access user must approve. A maintainer should confirm this.\n- **Docs:** updated the proposal, README, getting-started, the gate-2 runbook and the onboard-repo runbook with the three ways to start and the PAT trade-offs.\n- **Tests:**\n  - Added tests for connect, the `gh` fallback with a fake `gh` on `PATH`, token formatting, the startup path, the token-leak check and the merger PAT case.\n  - Three existing config-check tests now ignore the new auth line.\n\nOpen items:\n- CLAUDE.md still says GitHub access uses an App installation token. It is a protected path, so a maintainer must update it.\n- `ard init` still refuses a token outside dry-run; the plan didn't cover it.\n- For fine-grained tokens, only contents, issues and pull requests are verified, because checks and statuses read can't be probed without a commit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":920,"cache_read_input_tokens":85247,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":920},"output_tokens":719,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65048bc8-546a-4025-a94f-356c42be7752","uuid":"a4b4f1ca-5751-4edf-9f5c-99da8d14b2ae","timestamp":"2026-11-25T20:59:10.496Z","request_id":"req_011ChQKPGJcnq2SY6hwGYrc6"}
